SUMMARY:Schuylkill River Series: Pottstown-Royersford
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point hike\, the next in our Schuylkill series\,
  between Pottsville and Royersford.\nAfter meeting at Royersford\, we will
  shuttle with as few vehicles as possible to the start.\nWe'll start by fo
 llowing a small creek greenway\, then a bit of Schuylkill River Trail\, bu
 t we must deviate from it because the 422 crossing is not yet open.\nWe'll
  use parallel roads on the opposite side of the river including another co
 uple of parks and a cemetery to get to the next bit of the trail.\nWe'll c
 ontinue along the trail\, but deviate a couple of times to check out diffe
 rent side trails. We will be doing the Sanatoga Preserve as well as Indepe
 ndence Park Trail\, then the Royersford Trestle to the end.\nDistance will
  be about 15 miles. If needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374.
